  "id": "analytic-psychology",
  "term": "analytic psychology",
  "definition": "In this historical source, analytic psychology means a general psychological approach that studies the mind by breaking complex mental states into simpler elements or factors. It especially refers to analysis carried out through introspection and is contrasted with descriptive, genetic, and experimental psychology.",
